  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=5{x}^{2}-7.$ Let's first calculate the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2}-7)=10x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the slope of the tangent at our point is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{\u2032}(3)=10(3)=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the tangent is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(38) & =30(x-3) \\\\ y & =30x-90+38 \\\\ y & =30x-52.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find where the tangent line intercepts the $x$-axis, we set $y=0$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =30x-52 \\\\ x & =\\frac{26}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(\\frac{26}{15},0).$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
